#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f5b59d4-11de-519e-99fb-5490018d5225" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Function's Root Using the Newton-Raphson Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "5e109212-d6e7-53aa-af4f-e5698276cb13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090169}] :question/id #uuid "d82ea011-ddd7-5eaf-8739-fbc1e56a9b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-255829" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that the function $f(x) = e^{x} - 4x^{2}$ has a root in the interval $[0, 1]$, use the Netwon-Raphson process starting from $x_{0} = 1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.$x \\approx$\n{{field-1}}" :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f5b59d4-11de-519e-99fb-5490018d5225" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Function's Root Using the Newton-Raphson Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "2588342d-bc1f-5cd6-b82f-cac73690746c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090173}] :question/id #uuid "618793c9-3aaf-5791-81a7-b32bf3d17faa" :question/math-academy-id "q-256616" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that the function $f(x) = e^{x} - 3x$ has a root in the interval $[0, 1]$, use the Newton-Raphson process starting from $x_{0} = 0.2$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to three decimal places.$x \\approx$\n{{field-1}}\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"limitations-of-newtons-method\"></a>" :question/requires-calculator true}]}
